            <ArticleTitle>Trichobezoars.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>281-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Trichobezoars are a rare cause of upper gastrointestinal symptoms and most commonly occur in young females with trichophagia. A case, occurring in a 19 year old woman, complicated by transient pancreatitis and jejunal perforation, is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
